WEBVTT

00:10:26.371 --> 00:10:30.412
And one of the things she said to me,
she kept going to the father.

00:10:30.621 --> 00:10:32.496
She kept saying, your father,

00:10:32.496 --> 00:10:36.287
he's a Vietnam vet or he's troubled
or he's you know.

00:10:36.287 --> 00:10:39.954
And I kept saying, like, oh, yeah, my
father is not in my life. He's nothing.

00:10:39.954 --> 00:10:44.496
He's nothing. He's not anything. And she
said to me, well, you were wounded.

00:10:44.496 --> 00:10:48.412
Your father was wounded. And when
you have a parent who's wounded

00:10:48.746 --> 00:10:52.704
and who hasn't healed his or her wounds,
you you as the child,

00:10:52.704 --> 00:10:54.079
you're wounded in the same place.

00:10:54.579 --> 00:10:56.787
And so you're going to have
to heal that wounds.

00:10:57.579 --> 00:11:01.162
And the way she talked to me about it is
that there will be times in your life